The fix makes inline code markdown choose a backtick delimiter longer than the longest consecutive backtick run in the content. Existing normal inline code still renders without padding, while code containing backticks is wrapped with a longer delimiter and one space of padding so SystemVerilog macro text like `` `define ... `` and token-paste sequences with triple backticks render correctly.

